  "body": "The remaining part of #692, after #705 (feature graph + pick API) and #709 (every viewport picker on the rule).\n\n## Audit\nThe full table is on the issue: https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/issues/692#issuecomment-6801617642. In short, on main bdd29e00 every point of the issue was met and pinned except the four below (two fixed here, two still owed):\n\n| Point | Before | This PR |\n|---|---|---|\n| MCP `locate_part` mate ids | bypassed the rule: `fixture_tools::locate_part` parsed ids with `parse_feature_id` and never called `check_pickable`, so a vertex along a round rim or inside a face became a mate point | runs `pick::check_pickable` like every other MCP pick (`mcp::pick::pick_of`); refused by name |\n| User docs note on what a click picks | missing | new \"What a click picks\" section in `site/content/guide/operations.md` |\n| Circle/arc centre picks | the API's centre tier, no page asks for it | **still owed - waits for #759** (draft); not touched |\n| User-switchable \"pick through\" mode, off by default and shown as such | API only (`PickQuery::through`); the viewport always sends `through: false` (`feature_click::query_at`) and offers no control | **still owed**; not touched (a new viewport control; the decision record explains why it is not in this fix) |\n\nCorrection to the first audit: the pick-through row said \"met (API)\"; the issue asks for a mode the user can turn on, so it is still owed (corrected on the issue: https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/issues/692#issuecomment-6803948226).\n\nEverything else (faces, feature edges, feature points, hidden geometry, perspective/ortho, snap order by the tool's kinds, every UI picker incl. fixture locate, MCP list/set picks, degenerate input) is already pinned by `feature_pick::*`, `feature_pick_wire::*`, `one_pick_rule::*` and `mcp_pick::listed_chains_and_vertices_follow_the_one_pick_rule` - names in the audit table.\n\n## What changed\n- `crates/app/src/mcp/fixture_tools.rs`: `locate_part` checks each mate id with `pick::check_pickable` (3 lines).\n- `crates/app/tests/mcp_pick.rs`: pinning test `locate_part_refuses_a_mate_point_no_click_could_pick`; the boss STL writer is now a helper shared with `listed_chains_and_vertices_follow_the_one_pick_rule`.\n- `site/content/guide/operations.md`: \"What a click picks\".\n- `docs/decisions/692-pick-rule-rest.md`: why the check sits at the MCP door, why no pick-through control in the viewport, why centres wait for #759.\n\n## How tested\n- Pinning test `mcp_pick::locate_part_refuses_a_mate_point_no_click_could_pick`: FAILS with the fix stashed, passes with it.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main` on 3af6e765: green (app lib, mcp_pick, mcp_setup - 29 s).\n- By name: `feature_pick` 7/7, `feature_pick_wire` 4/4 (1 timing lane ignored), `mcp_pick` 4/4, UI `egui_app::tests::one_pick_rule` 6/6 (CWD crates/ui).\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean. No UI code changed.\n\nReview round (head 52f7a34b, test-only change): `locate_part_refuses_a_mate_point_no_click_could_pick` now also asserts that the refusal leaves the document unchanged (`get_job` - every model's placement/bounds, can_undo/can_redo - equal before and after), that a pickable mate (the boss's flat bottom on the vise top) succeeds and seats the boss at Z 20, and that one undo after it restores the placements (the refusal added no History step). Re-ran `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test mcp_pick` and `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`. The quick gate was not re-run: the change touches only this test file.\n\n## Still owed on #692 (this PR does not close it)\n- A \"pick through\" mode the user can turn on, off by default and shown as such - the API supports it, the viewport has no control.\n- Circle/arc centre picks - wait for #759.\n- The maintainer's hand GUI check of the viewport picks.\n\n## Not exercised\n- The maintainer's hand GUI check of the viewport picks (#709's note) - no GUI was launched; the UI behaviour is pinned by `one_pick_rule::*`.\n- No pick-through control is offered in the viewport (decision record); the API's `through` flag is pinned by `feature_pick::pick_through_does_pick_the_far_side_edge`.\n\nChangelog: MCP `locate_part` refuses a mate id no click could pick (a vertex along a round edge or inside a face), like the other pick tools; the user guide says what a click picks.\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nRefs #692 - still owed: the user pick-through mode, centre picks (#759) and the hand GUI check.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
